From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: Fix get_mclk_offset() for sun9i A80

get_mclk_offset() uses IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I_A80) to detect the
A80 SoC, but CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I_A80 does not exist anywhere in U-Boot
2024.01.  The correct Kconfig symbol for the Allwinner A80 (sun9i) is
CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I, which is defined in arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig.

Because the condition is never true, get_mclk_offset() always falls
through to the default return value (0x88), causing priv->mclkreg to be
computed as CCU_base + 0x88 + mmc_no*4 instead of the correct
CCU_base + 0x410 + mmc_no*4.

For eMMC (mmc2):
  Wrong:   0x06000000 + 0x88 + 8 = 0x06000090  (reserved CCU space)
  Correct: 0x06000000 + 0x410 + 8 = 0x06000418 (sd2_clk_cfg)

Every mmc_set_mod_clk() call writes the clock-select/divider value to
the wrong address (a no-op on reserved CCU space), leaving sd2_clk_cfg
unchanged at 24 MHz.  The clock dividers in CLKCR are reprogrammed for
400 kHz, but the module clock driving the controller stays at 24 MHz,
so the card actually sees 24 MHz during the initialization sequence.

More critically: because the sd2_clk_cfg register is never written, the
verify-then-re-enable sequence in mmc_config_clock() calls mmc_update_clk()
in the wrong controller state, causing the eMMC initialization to fail
entirely on sun9i A80 Cubieboard4 with "** Bad device specification mmc 1 **".

Also change mmc_rint_wait() and mmc_blk_probe() error paths from debug()
to pr_err() so initialization failures are visible on the serial console
at the default log level.

Signed-off-by: Copilot <copilot@github.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/mmc-uclass.c |  2 +-
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c  |  8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/mmc-uclass.c b/drivers/mmc/mmc-uclass.c
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/mmc-uclass.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/mmc-uclass.c
@@ -487,7 +487,7 @@ static int mmc_blk_probe(struct udevice *dev)
 	ret = mmc_init(mmc);
 	if (ret) {
-		debug("%s: mmc_init() failed (err=%d)\n", __func__, ret);
+		pr_err("%s: mmc_init() failed (err=%d)\n", __func__, ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
index 3333333..4444444 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -303,9 +303,11 @@ static int mmc_rint_wait(struct sunxi_mmc_priv *priv, struct mmc *mmc,
 		if ((get_timer(start) > timeout_msecs) ||
 		    (status & SUNXI_MMC_RINT_INTERRUPT_ERROR_BIT)) {
-			debug("%s timeout %x\n", what,
-			      status & SUNXI_MMC_RINT_INTERRUPT_ERROR_BIT);
+			pr_err("%s timeout rint=0x%x err=0x%x\n", what,
+			       status,
+			       status & SUNXI_MMC_RINT_INTERRUPT_ERROR_BIT);
 			return -ETIMEDOUT;
 		}
 
@@ -621,7 +623,7 @@ static unsigned get_mclk_offset(void)
 {
-	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I_A80))
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MACH_SUN9I))
 		return 0x410;
 
 	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUN50I_GEN_H6) || IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUNXI_GEN_NCAT2))
